	b. Performance
	Performance is the concept of performing a task or function, and this performance can be evaluated given the context and the need. Every performance can be evaluated regarding a fixed objective with key performance indicators (KPIs) defined beforehand. Some easy KPIs are : time taken to execute the task, precision of the task, cost of the task. When we want to evaluate a specific asset of the task, we create one or multiple KPIs. Performance assesments mostly rely on the human creating the KPIs, therefore the evaluations tend to have a great subjective component in their analysis.
	c. Machine learning
	Machine learning is the systematic study of algorithms and statistical models using computer systems that are able to learn and adapt without external instructions. Machine learning algorithms and models are made to learn from existing patterns in data and make inferences using past experience to draw conclusions. The algorithm(s) used are dependant on the problem and it's analysis needs, see fig. /href{graphique_...} for a quick summary on the methods used in ML.
